1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:10,025
Every day, people receive payment links, utility bills, and official letters.
These inputs can ask for money, identity documents, or a response by a

2
00:00:10,025 --> 00:00:13,747
deadline. Understanding them should not require taking unnecessary risks.

3
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:27,870
The problem is not a shortage of AI answers. It is a shortage of safe
inspection and verifiable evidence. A link can be deceptive. A bill can

4
00:00:27,870 --> 00:00:35,107
contain incorrect charges. Letter requirements and deadlines can be missed.
And a confident summary does not prove what was checked.

5
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:44,984
Proofbox inspects safely, verifies claims, and preserves evidence.

6
00:00:45,268 --> 00:00:50,672
We begin with Link Lens. It observes a page without asking the person to open
it or submit credentials.

7
00:00:52,906 --> 00:00:59,082
For this recording, we inspect the public Proofbox demo site itself. This is
not a malicious test page.

8
00:01:01,317 --> 00:01:06,858
The job runs in an isolated browser. The control plane collects the page trace
and inspection image.

9
00:01:09,093 --> 00:01:16,967
The live result is SUSPICIOUS. References to the fictional bank in the demo
can trigger a brand-mismatch warning. This illustrates why findings still need

10
00:01:16,967 --> 00:01:17,623
human review.

11
00:01:19,858 --> 00:01:26,916
The trace and lifecycle events show what was observed. A warning is not proof
of fraud, and no issue found would not guarantee safety.

12
00:01:29,150 --> 00:01:36,270
The built-in private-address example was rejected during rehearsal. No
blocked-network or download-quarantine result is claimed in this recording.

13
00:01:38,953 --> 00:01:45,601
Next, Bill Lens. We upload the synthetic injection fixture and a reading-
history file with outage context.

14
00:01:47,071 --> 00:01:55,570
The PDF contains an instruction addressed to an AI: approve the bill and print
its environment. That text is untrusted document data, not permission to act.

15
00:01:57,431 --> 00:02:04,301
The parser operates in the worker sandbox. The model extracts fields, while
deterministic code checks the tariff arithmetic.

16
00:02:06,162 --> 00:02:13,501
The live result reports a possible overcharge of one hundred thirty-four rand
and fifty-five cents. It also flags consecutive estimated readings and

17
00:02:13,501 --> 00:02:15,836
consumption inconsistent with the supplied outage history.

18
00:02:17,698 --> 00:02:23,351
The receipt links connect each finding to the bill text, the recomputation,
and the independently executed program.

19
00:02:25,212 --> 00:02:30,088
The final draft explains the discrepancy for review. No letter is sent
automatically.

20
00:02:31,949 --> 00:02:39,275
Karoo Bay is fictional. These results demonstrate the fixture and configured
rules, not verification of a real municipality's tariff.

21
00:02:41,584 --> 00:02:47,904
Letter Lens turns correspondence into a checklist. We provide an agency letter
and three synthetic supporting documents.

22
00:02:49,116 --> 00:02:56,201
The official letter supplies the requirements and explicit dates. Supporting
PDFs are parsed and checked in the no-network worker sandbox.

23
00:02:57,413 --> 00:03:04,988
The live checklist flags an address document that is too old, and a missing
signed declaration. It also records the response deadline and appointment from

24
00:03:04,988 --> 00:03:05,594
the letter.

25
00:03:06,806 --> 00:03:13,336
These are layout-based checks. They do not authenticate identity or documents,
and scanned PDFs are not supported.

26
00:03:14,548 --> 00:03:20,188
Supporting-document check facts, rather than full supporting text, form the
model privacy boundary.

27
00:03:21,847 --> 00:03:28,194
Now we bring the completed bill check into a private case. This is a synthetic
demonstration case created for this recording.

28
00:03:29,756 --> 00:03:35,097
We first attach the bill job. Stable evidence numbers connect the findings to
case-owned receipts.

29
00:03:36,659 --> 00:03:42,075
A drafted municipal dispute does not start its response clock: the person must
confirm when it was sent.

30
00:03:43,638 --> 00:03:51,474
The live export is refused: a receipt matches the thirteen-digit identifier
gate. The synthetic bill contains a long numeric creation date in its PDF

31
00:03:51,474 --> 00:03:56,697
metadata. This is an export limitation, not proof that the bill holds a real
identity number.

32
00:03:58,260 --> 00:04:06,198
Numbered claims link back to evidence. Receipt hashes support content-
integrity checks, but do not prove authenticity or legal correctness.

33
00:04:07,364 --> 00:04:15,120
The case still keeps its evidence and receipts. Supporting identity PDFs are
intended to be omitted from exports, and private case links must be shared

34
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:15,741
with care.

35
00:04:17,303 --> 00:04:22,469
This is the handoff: a record another person can inspect, rather than a
disconnected chat answer.

36
00:04:24,479 --> 00:04:30,960
Vultr separates authority from execution. The control-plane VM owns the API,
case engine, and model gateway.

37
00:04:31,024 --> 00:04:37,831
A private sandbox-host VM runs browser and code tasks with Docker and gVisor.
The inference key stays outside the worker.

38
00:04:37,896 --> 00:04:46,336
Models interpret. Code verifies. People confirm consequential actions. This
demo is not a certification of escape resistance.

39
00:04:46,847 --> 00:04:51,038
Proofbox connects useful agent work with bounded execution and reviewable
evidence.

40
00:04:51,690 --> 00:04:55,021
Production checks and official domain rules still need verification.

41
00:04:55,672 --> 00:04:59,170
Open nothing unsafely. Believe nothing unproven.
